# Security

- Never expose shell commands to the frontend.
- Never concatenate untrusted user input into shell command strings.
- Spawn yt-dlp / FFmpeg with `Command` + argv arrays only.
- Validate and sanitize all user input in Rust before process or DB work.
- Use typed interfaces between frontend and Rust; reject invalid payloads.
- Keep Tauri capabilities minimal; do not enable arbitrary shell or open FS beyond needed scopes.
- Resolve binary paths from settings or known locations — never from raw user shell fragments.
